ced). If the calling account had been revoked `role`, emits a {RoleRevoked} event. Requirements: - the caller must be `callerConfirmation`. May emit a {RoleRevoked} event."},"revokeRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Revokes `role` from `account`. If `account` had been granted `role`, emits a {RoleRevoked} event. Requirements: - the caller must have ``role``'s admin role. May emit a {RoleRevoked} event."},"supportsInterface(bytes4)":{"details":"Returns true if this contract implements the interface defined by `interfaceId`. See the corresponding https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-165#how-interfaces-are-identified[ERC section] to learn more about how these ids are created. This function call must use less than 30 000 gas."}},"title":"AurixRewardClaim","version":1},"userdoc":{"kind":"user","methods":{"APPROVER_MANAGER_ROLE()":{"notice":"Role permitted to grant and revoke APPROVER_ROLE."},"APPROVER_ROLE()":{"notice":"Role whose current members may sign reward authorizations."},"CAMPAIGN_MANAGER_ROLE()":{"notice":"Role permitted to create and narrowly update campaigns."},"MAX_CLAIM_INTERVAL()":{"notice":"Maximum campaign claim interval."},"MIN_CLAIM_INTERVAL()":{"notice":"Minimum campaign claim interval."},"PAUSER_ROLE()":{"notice":"Role permitted to pause the contract."},"REWARD_AUTHORIZATION_TYPEHASH()":{"notice":"Canonical EIP-712 type hash for RewardAuthorization."},"TREASURY_ROLE()":{"notice":"Role permitted to recover tokens under paused-only restrictions."},"campaigns(bytes32)":{"notice":"Campaign configuration and accounting by campaign ID."},"claimReward((address,uint256,bytes32,bytes32,uint256,uint256,uint256),bytes)":{"notice":"Claims a reward using a current Approver's EIP-712 signature."},"constructor":{"notice":"Initializes the immutable reward token and separated operational roles."},"createCampaign(bytes32,uint256,uint256,uint64,uint64,uint64,bool)":{"notice":"Creates a new campaign."},"eip712Name()":{"notice":"Returns the EIP-712 domain name."},"eip712Ve